/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    Region escape THROUGH A FUNCTION BOUNDARY: a function launders a rabbit-scoped
    series out by returning its own parameter (the checker's ReturnDepthSignature
    propagates the argument's depth to the call site, so this is still caught).

    The outward-only region-store invariant refuses it: the value lives in a
    shorter-lived rabbit region than its destination, so it would dangle after
    the rabbit's Done. pops that region. Nothing below ever executes. */

Bind series of number to smuggle, given (the series of number s):
    return s.
Done.

Define outer as a series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    outer becomes Cast smuggle on (inner).
Done.
Define outer-count as the number of outer.
